"/docs/components/chip-39","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#controlled-selection","content":"Use `selectedKeys` and `onSelectionChange` when another part of the page\nneeds to own the selected filter state."},"308":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-40","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#sizes","content":"Compare the supported `sm`, `md`, and `lg` sizes. Set `size` on `ChipGroup`\nso every Chip inherits one consistent size."},"309":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-41","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#disabled","content":"Disable individual options with `disabledKeys` when some values are unavailable."},"310":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-42","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#truncation","content":"By default, long labels truncate visually when space is constrained, while\nthe complete accessible value remains available."},"311":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-43","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#empty-state","content":"Give an empty collection useful guidance, then let the user add the first\nvalue. Removable items continue to be owned by the collection."},"312":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-44","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#menu-filter-trigger","content":"Use `ChipButton` for Chip presentation without collection semantics.\n`MenuTrigger` continues to own open state, focus, and keyboard behavior."},"313":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-45","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#content","content":"Use a string for a simple label. For icons or other composed content, wrap the\nvisible label in `Text` and provide `textValue` for the accessible name. See\n**Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips** above."},"314":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-46","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#selection-and-removal","content":"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."},"315":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-47","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#layout-and-sizing","content":"Set `size` on `ChipGroup` to keep a collection consistent. `ChipList` wraps by\ndefault and accepts layout props for custom arrangements. See **Sizes**."},"316":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-48","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#button-composition","content":"Use `ChipButton` when Chip presentation is needed without collection semantics.\nCompose it with components such as `MenuTrigger`; those components continue to\nown open state, focus, and keyboard behavior. See **Menu filter trigger**."},"317":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-49","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#accessibility","content":"Use `Label` or `aria-label` to name the `ChipGroup`; this names the collection,\nnot its individual Chips."},"318":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-50","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#accessibility","content":"Give each Chip a visible label, `textValue`, or `aria-label`. Use `textValue`\nwhen a Chip contains icons, composed content, or a render prop."},"319":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-51","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#accessibility","content":"Use a descriptive group label so removal actions can be announced clearly."},"320":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-52","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#accessibility","content":"Keep the visible label and the accessible value synchronized."},"321":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-53","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#accessibility","content":"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."},"322":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-54","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#best-practices","content":"Keep labels concise and let them truncate only when the available width requires it."},"323":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-55","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#best-practices","content":"Prefer groups of three or more related values."},"324":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-56","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#best-practices","content":"Keep one size per group."},"325":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-57","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#best-practices","content":"Let `ChipList` wrap instead of forcing a single horizontal line."},"326":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-58","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#best-practices","content":"Use removable Chips for user-added filters and tokens."},"327":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-59","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#best-practices","content":"For menu filters, use `ChipButton` with `MenuTrigger` and provide the chevron explicitly."},"328":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-60","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#a-chipgroup-has-no-accessible-name","content":"Add a visible `Label` to the group or provide `aria-label`. For an individual Chip\nwith composed content, provide a visible label, `textValue`, or `aria-label`."},"329":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-61","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#the-remove-action-does-not-update-the-ui","content":"Add `onRemove` to `ChipGroup` and remove the returned keys from the collection\nowned by your application."},"330":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-62","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#a-composed-label-is-not-truncating-correctly","content":"Keep the label in `Text`, preserve `textValue`, and constrain the available width\nof the surrounding layout. Truncation is visual; the complete accessible value\nshould remain available."},"331":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-63","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#the-menu-trigger-does-not-look-like-a-chip","content":"Use `ChipButton` inside `MenuTrigger`, include the visible value, and add a\ntrailing chevron to communicate that the control opens a menu."},"332":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-64","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#props","content":"For a menu trigger, the button and menu are composed as siblings inside\n`MenuTrigger`:"},"333":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"page","content":"CircularProgress","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress"},"334":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-0","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/circular-progress","content":"A circular progress indicator shows determinate progress of an operation over time"},"335":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-1","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#installation","content":"Installation"},"336":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-2","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#examples","content":"Examples"},"337":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-3","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#default","content":"Default"},"338":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-4","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"339":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-5","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#emphasis","content":"Emphasis"},"340":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-6","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"341":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-7","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#aria-support","content":"ARIA Support"},"342":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-8","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#props","content":"Props"},"343":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-9","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#circularprogress","content":"CircularProgress"},"344":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-10","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#default","content":"A basic determinate progress indicator with a label and helper text."},"345":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-11","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#sizes","content":"Four circle diameters are available: `sm` (64px), `md` (96px), `lg` (128px), and `xl` (160px)."},"346":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-12","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#emphasis","content":"Use the `emphasis` prop to communicate status: `success`, `warning`, or `critical`. When omitted, the default teal fill is used."},"347":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-13","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#aria-support","content":"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"},"348":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-14","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#aria-support","content":"`aria-valuenow` reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"},"349":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-15","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#aria-support","content":"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"},"350":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-16","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#aria-support","content":"`aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"},"351":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-17","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/circular-progress#aria-support","content":"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"},"352":{"id":"/docs/components/circular-progress-18","page_id":"/docs/components/circular-progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/circular-progr