o its trigger, with an optional arrow"},"1604":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-17","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#features","content":"Flips and shifts to stay in the viewport"},"1605":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-18","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#features","content":"Configurable open and close delays"},"1606":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-19","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#default","content":"Use it with `TooltipTrigger`, which wraps both the tooltip content and a focusable element such as a `Button`. The tooltip appears on hover and focus."},"1607":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-20","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#custom-anchor","content":"To position a tooltip relative to a different focusable element, use the `triggerRef` prop. `TooltipTrigger` still handles showing and hiding on hover and focus."},"1608":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-21","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#customization","content":"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."},"1609":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-22","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#keyboard","content":"Key"},"1610":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-23","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#keyboard","content":"Action"},"1611":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-24","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#keyboard","content":"`Tab`"},"1612":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-25","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#keyboard","content":"Moves focus to the focusable element and shows the tooltip"},"16