er"],[1114,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[351,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[953,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[248,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1172,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[349,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[951,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[950,"`aria-valuenow` reflects the current value"],[348,"`aria-valuenow` reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[952,"`aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`)"],[350,"`aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[1852,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[153,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[233,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[303,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[321,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[299,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard 